-- EXPERIMENT extraction-throughput query -- Sema translation of
-- query/flockmtl/Q103.sql, arm (b): VERBATIM PROMPT.
--
-- The instruction text is byte-identical to the flockmtl / LOTUS / Palimpzest
-- arms, so this is the strictly fair prompt-parity comparison. Its known
-- problem is documented rather than worked around: with exactly this wording
-- Sema's semantic map returns empty strings and stray fragments (observed on a
-- 3-row fixture: "", ":-(", ""), which looks like substring-scraping of the JSON
-- response rather than parsing it. Expect a low F1 here for a PARSING reason,
-- not a model-quality reason -- see Q103_question.sql for the arm that isolates
-- that, and report the two together.
--
-- Column order matters: MovieEvaluator._evaluate_q103 reads column 0 as
-- reviewId and column 1 as the predicted label, canonicalising anything
-- containing POSITIVE/NEGATIVE.
--
-- Sema's semantic map is a projection-position s'...' expression. Note it is
-- NOT usable as a boolean outside WHERE: inside CASE WHEN it evaluates as a map
-- and fails with a BOOL conversion error, which is why Q4/Q8 cannot be ported
-- directly. (Do not write the jinja model placeholder in these comments -- the
-- runner renders the whole file, so it would be substituted inside the comment.)
SELECT
  reviewId,
  s'Classify the sentiment of this movie review as exactly one of POSITIVE or NEGATIVE. Answer with only the single word POSITIVE or NEGATIVE: {reviewText}' AS predicted_sentiment
FROM reviews_2000;
